/*
Set of events where group of kids adopts you as a pet. not sure how "oneoff" the event should be,
if I really want to make it more of a permanent thing the kids should probably become named NPCs though not learning their names could be nice even if a little unrealistic
Jean, Kallen and Noel could work as names if necessary
I could make them have all sorts of mundane drama and stuff that they could talk to you about while training you and then you could decide

Name they use for you could be based on your hair colour so:
blackie, brownie, coco, hazel, muffin, sandy, goldie, snowy, blu, bacon, ruby, red, moss, pink, peach
or fifi if there isn't a good colour based one


*/



<!--

There probably should be a somewhat fixed order to how you get trained so that the events can rely on you already having certain trainings at sufficient levels.
For some things always checking if you've completed a training or not should be fine.
Obedience could be a thing to always check, it'd basically be trio specific submissive/defiant score, there will probably be some situations where having it as a separate makes it worth not just using $submissive.
I feel like always wearing clothes should be possible so nudity training would be another thing to always check.

Not speaking and going on walks with some sort of leash and collar are essential so shouldn't be skippable.
Not learning to do some "tricks" doesn't seem interesting(to make it actually require some training instead of just obediently doing whatever is said the trio should read that they should use commands in another language to avoid confusion with normal speech) but not exactly super important so maybe not required for any other training but no way to make the trio give up on teaching you at least some commands.
Wearing a tail of some sort would be required for shaking it to indicate happiness and having it get janked. Shaking could be done without the tail(actually starting off without tailplug could make getting arousal from an already habitual action a nice surprise), any janking could probably be replaced with either a slap or nothing happening while a <<tailwag>>/<<buttshake>> widget for reacting to presence or lack of buttplug seems fine so the plug'd be optional but tailwagging required.
	Not sure how anal shield should affect things
	Also unremovable(without assistance from the trio) tailplug could be interesting but mainly since it'd mean the trio would have to manage when you poop, if I did that I'd prefer to do it in a way that avoids focusing on actual pooping(not into scat) so something like constipation effect that you get if you have something blocking your anus for too long without release and the release being something like "The trio briefly remove your tailplug to allow you to poop before putting it back in and locking it up."
	I'd prefer having a tail from a transformation not matter but making it so that it'd be easy to make it matter shouldn't be too hard since I'll already have no tail or plug tail conditions.
Moving on all fours(with tool assistance?) would make tail wagging more obvious and probably mean adjusting the wording of every pet event which could be reasonably doable with some widgets and since it'd be weird to split events to post/pre allfours training so it'll be somewhat optional.
Eating like a dog'd be pretty self contained so other than getting rewarded with some sort of treats(which would be fed by hand) there'd be no effect on anything else so not required. Waiting for permission to eat and getting used to dogfood could be things to practice.
Marking/Peeing definetly optional since it's watersports, mainly relevant for walks but also for using a litterbox(or refusing to do so and peeing wherever).


So rough training order:
Nonverbal and (Obedience) as part of linear intro events
Tailwagging/Communication
Tricks1
Collar
Walks
(Tricks2, food permission)
(Tail)
(Allfours)
(Dogfood)
(Nudity)
(Marking)
(Litterbox use)

Getting the required trainings out of the way asap does make sense but risks making player assume eveything is required. Somehow letting the player choose which training to do could help... In general letting you have some control over what activity you're doing would be nice but not sure how it could work for most of the optional trainings, besides absolutely not wanting to do training doesn't seem likely so maybe it's more of you can react badly or refuse training(even required ones) and the next time they'll try something else before trying again and only if you keep refusing do they consider giving up (unless it's a required one, suggesting you just stop showing up could be an option then but doesn't seem necessary). Having a gentler and more firm intros to trainings with the initial attempt being based on obedience level while new attempts after refusing would use the opposite type intro(if there are more than two then current obedience based intro followed by low opposite and high opposite intros seems like a pattern to use, 4 or more attempts seems too many) seems like a decent idea.

Should keep in mind that there are a bunch of events that aren't exactly part of training that should happen.

How you get dressed up as a dog is a question, at first the idea was that you'd dress appropriately before meeting up with the trio but having the trio do it for you after they see you could be interesting too though would they also remove the stuff when you're done?
	Telling you to wear x when coming to meet them would be kind of weird and OOC as would punishing you for not doing so, complaining about you losing things given to you would be more natural though for tail slightly OOC but tolerable, for not wearing clothes there should just be positive reinforcement where you get praised/rewarded for not wearing too much but if you do they just undress you if you're ok with that.

Should doing things(moving on all fours) without training be an option? 
Will binds with elbow and knee pads to somewhat comfortably force moving on all fours end up being a thing?

-->
<!-- 
Would petplay lewd stat that gives control make sense? Where proactively behaving like a pet will give control? 
Ferality, Wildness, Spontaneity, Canineness, Dogness, Petness, Pettability, Domestication, Tameness, Housebreaking, Conditioning, Habituation, Discipline, Pacification, Docility, Pliantness, Chastisement.
Docility or tameness seem good if the idea of being proactive about it isn't important, can't find a good word for just freely acting like an animal that doesn't have wrong connotations. Could just go with petness since even if it doesn't fit in with the rest that well it's closest to the meaning I want.
-->
<<set $petscore to 0>><!-- this is for how "in character" you are, probably replaced with $petness -->
<<set $petness to 0>><!-- how used to acting like a pet you are -->
<<set $petobedience to 0>><!-- obedience decides how strict the trio is -->
<<set $triogender to "m">>
<<set $peteventbag to []>>


<<set $petname to "doggie">>
<<set _s to {$}>>
<<set $pettraining to {obedience:0,nonverbal:{0},tricks:0,collar:0,tail:0,nudity:0,eating:0,marking:0,walking:0,}>>




<<set $trio to {name:"",love:0,lust:0,dom:0,health:"good",grades:"normal",gender:"m",relationships:{}}>>
<<set $jean to $trio>>
<<set $kallen to $trio>>
<<set $noel to $trio>>




<<if $peteventbag.length is 0>>
  <<if $petname is "doggie">><<set $peteventbag.push("naming")>><</if>>
  <<for _i to 7;_i gt 0;_i-->>


<<run $peteventbag.shuffle>>


You see a group of kids/boys/girls hanging around

